-- title:
--   Supersingular chart of the level-q model with its q+1 nodes
-- statement:
--   Data and hypotheses. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the set of nonunits of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over the residue field of $A$ (this field being the subfield generated over the residue field by the two Laurent series $j$ and $j\circ q^{M'}$-expansion), and let `hW` assert that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of those places $w$ that are rational (the structure map from the base field onto the residue field of $w$ is surjective), lie in the affine geometric locus, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j)\in \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$. Let `hle` assert the inclusion $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(M')\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the base-changed full level-$M'$ modular function field into the base-changed function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H=\ker(\mathrm{ZMod}(q^2M')^\times\to \mathrm{ZMod}(q)^\times)$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(M')$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A,M')$: a valuation subring of integers, a surjective ring map to the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, compatibility with $A$ and with its residue map, the existence for every nonzero $f$ of a scalar $c$ with $c\cdot f$ an integer of nonzero residue, and compatibility of divisors under the place map. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that this reduction is computed coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients lies in $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(M')$, that element is an integer of $R_0$ and its residue is the Laurent series obtained from $y$ by reducing coefficients modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, that is, a supersingular place.
--
--   Small-constants hypotheses. $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ with $\pi_0\in A$; writing $A\cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require $A\cap k_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` requires every $a\in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   Auxiliary primes and parameters. $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Base-layer hypotheses. $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$, and $\varpi_b\ne 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The level field. With $k_0$ acting on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'/k_0$ characterised by the stated coefficient condition: $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$. Moreover $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, and the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (2) ($W_0$ lies over $s$.) For every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in the full level-$M'$ modular function field whose base change is an integer of $R_0$, if $g$ has no poles where $j$ has none (for every place $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(M')$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$) and the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that image and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (3) ($W_0$ is level-stable.) For every $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f\in\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with both $f$ and $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f$ in $F_0$: $f\in W_0$ if and only if $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f\in W_0$.
--
--   (4) (The affine chart.) There exist a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (4a) the structure map of $A_b$ into $B$ is the inclusion, i.e. the image of $a\in A_b$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ equals the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$;
--
--   (4b) $B$ is contained in the compositum $k_0(K_b)\sqcup F_0$ (the join of the intermediate field generated over $k_0$ by the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$), and every element of that compositum is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$ (so $B$ has that compositum as fraction field);
--
--   (4c) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (4d) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; $\varpi_b$ maps to a prime element of $B$; and $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime, in the sense that $f\in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$ in $B$;
--
--   (4e) the image of $j$ lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under all the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (4f) (the chart separates $s$ from the cusps) there is $b\in B\cap F_0$ such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which restricts to $A$ on $k_0$, contains $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and for which $j$ is a unit in the sense that every monic polynomial over $k_0\cap A$ evaluated at $j$ lies in $V$ outside the maximal ideal, one has $b\notin V$;
--
--   (4g) (the chart separates $s$ from the other supersingular places) for every $s'\in W$ with $s'\ne s$ there is $b\in B\cap F_0$ such that every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ restricting to $A$ on $k_0$ and lying over $s'$ in the sense of (2) satisfies $b\notin V$;
--
--   (4h) (Drinfeld-curve description of the special fibre) for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, every proof that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ into the fixed field $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ of the Drinfeld function field under the action of $C_s$, such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ is $2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$; the kernel of $\rho$ is $\varpi_b B$; $\rho$ restricted to $A_b$ is the residue map of $A$ followed by the structure map of $\kappa$; every element of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ is a quotient $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B$, $\rho(h)\neq0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of the elements of the fixed field lying in the image of the coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ in the Drinfeld function field; and $\rho$ intertwines the level automorphisms with the Drinfeld $H$-action: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ such that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $f\in B$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}f\in B$, the image under $\rho$ of the latter equals $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   (4i) (The nodes.) There is a finite set $\mathrm{nodes}$ of subrings of $F_0$ of cardinality $q+1$ with the following properties.
--
--   (i) The level automorphisms permute $\mathrm{nodes}$: for all $\zeta$, all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and all $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$ there is $O'\in\mathrm{nodes}$ such that for $f$ with $f$ and $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f$ in $F_0$ one has $f\in O$ if and only if its image lies in $O'$; and the action is transitive in the form: for every $\zeta$ and all $O,O'\in\mathrm{nodes}$ there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ realising the same equivalence between membership in $O$ and in $O'$.
--
--   (ii) Distinct nodes are distinguished by units: for $O\ne O'$ in $\mathrm{nodes}$ there is $f\in F_0$ belonging to both which is a nonunit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$.
--
--   (iii) (Every point of the chart over $s$ is either a point of $B$ or specialises into a node.) For every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ restricting to $A$ on $k_0$ and lying over $s$ in the sense of (2), either every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or there is $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$ all of whose elements lie in $V$, with every nonunit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   (iv) Each node $O\in\mathrm{nodes}$ satisfies: $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $O$; every $f\in O$ is congruent to a constant, in the sense that there is $x\in k_0\cap A$ with image in $O$ such that $f-x$ is a nonunit of $O$; and there exist a natural number $E_0\ge 1$ together with: a unit $v$ of $k_0\cap A$ (i.e. $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\,v$; a witness that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$; elements $c_x,c_y\in O$; a unit $u$ of $O$; and an isomorphism of rings $\iota$ from the completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ over the completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, i.e. the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by $(XY-\pi_0^{E_0})$; together with units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota$ sends constants from $k_0\cap A$ to the corresponding constants of the crossing model; $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$ for the two coordinates $U,V$ of the crossing model; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, whereas $c_x$, when in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal.
--
--   Furthermore, for each node $O$ there exist:
--
--   — a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, restricting to $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, admitting an element $t$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ not; and such that $W_x$ computes reductions: for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ field whose base change is an integer of $R_0$ and which has no poles where $j$ has none, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ vanishes, and if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $g$ lies in $O$ and, for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ with image in $O$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, the difference of the two is a nonunit of $O$;
--
--   — a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ all of whose elements lie in $B$ and in $O$, all of whose elements have no poles where $j$ has none (as places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at the nonunits of $O$ (an element $f\in F_0$ lies in $O$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h\in O$), $F_0$ is the field of fractions of $B_x$, and $B_x$ is generated as a ring by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set $T$; and $B_x$ contains an element $b$ such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ restricting to $A$ on $k_0$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, for which $j$ is a unit in the sense of (4f), and which fails to contain some element of $O$, one has $b\notin V$.
--
--   This is the construction, at a supersingular point $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$, of the local model of the semistable reduction of the full level-$q^2M'$ modular curve over the small-constants field $k_0$: a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ on the level field $F_0$ lying over $s$ and level-stable, an affine chart $B$ over $A_b$ which is formally smooth, finitely presented, of relative dimension one in the fibre, with special fibre identified with an affine Drinfeld curve quotient $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ equivariantly for the $\Gamma_0(M')$-action, together with the $q+1$ nodes of the chart, each with its $uv=\pi_0^{E_0}$ crossing description after completion. It is the version of the construction for the level field given by the $q$-expansion-coefficient characterisation, and feeds the identification of the adic completions of the stalks of the normal model at the node charts.
